# PAM stack for the "dropbear" service, used by phosphor-ipmi-host's
# pamUserCheckAuthenticate() (pam_authenticate + pam_acct_mgmt) to verify
# IPMI user credentials.
#
# Do NOT list pam_ipmicheck.so / pam_ipmisave.so here: both implement only
# pam_sm_chauthtok (they belong in a "password" stack). Placing them in the
# auth/account stacks made PAM log "unable to resolve symbol:
# pam_sm_authenticate / pam_sm_setcred / pam_sm_acct_mgmt" on every IPMI login
# (auth still succeeded via pam_unix). pam_unix does the real work.
auth     required   pam_unix.so
account  required   pam_unix.so
